---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<section class="mb-5">
		<h1>MICRONEEDLING (ReNu Pen®)</h1>
		<p class="text-xl bg-[#EEE8E0] px-2">POST-TREATMENT INSTRUCTIONS</p>
	</section>
	<section>
		<div class="separation">
			<h2>WHAT TO EXPECT</h2>
			<h2>DAY 1–2</h2>
			<p>	• Mild redness (similar to a sunburn) <br>
				• Mild swelling <br>
				• Warmth <br>
				• Skin sensitivity <br>
			</p>
			<p>Apply cool compresses as needed for comfort.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>DAY 2–5</h2>
			<p>	• Skin may feel tight or dry. <br>
				• Mild peeling or flaking is expected. <br>
				• Do not pick or exfoliate the treated skin. <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>FIRST 72 HOURS</h2>
			<p>Avoid:</p>
			<p>	• Retinoids <br>
				• AHAs and BHAs <br>
				• Vitamin C <br>
				• Makeup <br>
				• Strenuous exercise <br>
				• Hot showers <br>
				• Hot tubs <br>
				• Steam rooms <br>
				• Saunas <br>
				• Direct sun exposure <br>
				• Touching your face unnecessarily <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>HOME CARE</h2>
			<h2>NIGHT 1</h2>
			<p>	1. Alastin Gentle Cleanser <br>
				2. Alastin Regenerating Skin Nectar <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>DAYS 2–14</h2>
			<h2>MORNING</h2>
			<p>	1. Alastin Gentle Cleanser <br>
				2. Alastin Regenerating Skin Nectar <br>
				3. UV Skin Sunscreen (Mineral SPF 50) <br>
			</p>
			<h2>EVENING</h2>
			<p>	1. Alastin Gentle Cleanser <br>
				2. Alastin Regenerating Skin Nectar <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>AFTER DAY 14</h2>
			<p>Resume your normal maintenance skincare routine unless otherwise instructed by your provider.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>POSSIBLE ADVERSE REACTIONS</h2>
			<h2>COMMON</h2>
			<p>	• Redness <br>
				• Mild swelling <br>
				• Dryness <br>
				• Tightness <br>
				• Mild peeling <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>LESS COMMON</h2>
			<p>	• HSV activation (cold sore) <br>
				• Post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation <br>
				• Allergic reaction to topical serums or skincare products <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>RARE</h2>
			<p>	• Infection (increasing redness, warmth, drainage, or pustules after 72 hours) <br>
				• Granuloma formation <br>
				• Keloid formation <br>
				• Prolonged erythema lasting longer than 72 hours <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>CONTACT kiwiMEDSPA IMMEDIATELY IF YOU EXPERIENCE</h2>
			<p>	• Blistering or burns <br>
				• Severe or worsening pain lasting longer than 48 hours <br>
				• Increasing redness after initial improvement <br>
				• Drainage, pus, or fever <br>
				• Persistent or significant skin discoloration <br>
				• Vision changes <br>
				• Any unexpected or concerning reaction <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>RECOMMENDED TREATMENT SCHEDULE</h2>
			<p>	• 3–6 treatment sessions <br>
				• Treatments every 4–6 weeks <br>
			</p>
			<p>Maintenance treatments may be recommended based on your provider's recommendations.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>QUESTIONS?</h2>
			<p>kiwiMEDSPA</p>
			<p>Medical Weight Loss &amp; Aesthetics</p>
			<p>Dr. Sergio Angel, MD</p>
			<p>Dr. Allie Angel, MD</p>
			<p>470-310-8155</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
